[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. The reports say otherwise. We merged them on
subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and every one of them has a
subject about a wrong date, so three different problems went into one ticket. Each now has a ticket
of its own:

- [**parser** · #1](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/1): the shared parser reads day-first
  dates month first, so day and month swap.
- [**hint** · #2](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/2): the booking-v3 form hints MM/DD and
  reads DD/MM, so day and month swap. A parser fix does not touch it.
- [**one-day move** · #3](https://github.com/skligerman/mega/issues/3): the date moves by one day
  across time zones. No swap explains it, and a parser fix does not close it.

<Callout kind="warn">
The fix queued for #4471 is the parser fix. It closes #1 only.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table counts each report once, under the cause its tenant and channel give it. The one-day
moves in the note under it are filed under `parser` there, and tracked on their own in #3.

## How to tell them apart

Not by subject: all three share the same subject lines. Not by intake's tag: it guesses from the
reporter's browser, not from the tenant. Look at the tenant, the way in, and the body.

- **parser (#1)**: a day-first tenant, by app, email or the booking-v2 form. The body names two
  dates with day and month swapped: "8 December is now 12 August".
- **hint (#2)**: a booking-v3 tenant (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour), by the form. The
  body looks the same as parser, but the hint under the date field told the person to type the
  month first. The form's hint, or how it reads the date, has to change.
- **one-day move (#3)**: the date moves by one day, or differs between two places: "Client in
  Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." The desk notes list these as `oneDayMove`.

## For the desk

- Before you merge into a big ticket, check that the cause matches, not just the subject. The
  explorer on [triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows the cause for each pair.
- When a desk note says some reports read differently, give them a ticket of their own, not only a
  footnote.

